{
  "case_id": "2019-18-260",
  "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Elbert Lin)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LIN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case is not about whether the releases from Maui's underground injection wells should be regulated at all but how. They are already regulated under several existing state and federal environmental programs, including the Clean Water Act's nonpoint source program. But is a Clean Water Act point source permit also required? The question is where the line falls between the Clean Water Act's federal point source program and its state law nonpoint source program. And the answer is in the text. The text defines a point source as a discernible, confined, and discrete conveyance, and it thereby makes clear that the trigger for point"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Elbert Lin)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LIN: That's right, because groundwater is a nonpoint source. And if the groundwater is -- in this case is diffusely flowing through the ground and that's what carries the pollutants to the navigable waters --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The first point I'd like to make about the -- the definition of discharge of a pollutant is that the combination of the words \"to\" and \"from\" import more than either term in isolation; that the statute defines the term \"discharge of a pollutant\" to mean any addition of a pollutant to navigable waters or to the ocean from a point source. And, for example, if at my home I pour whiskey from a bottle into a flask and then I bring the flask to a party at a different location and I pour whiskey into the punch bowl there, nobody would say that I had added whiskey to the punch from the bottle."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: And in -- in your test, any little bit of groundwater is enough to break the chain?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: Yes. Now -- now the hypothetical --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What's the difference between the groundwater and the land?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Why -- why --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Henkin",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Clean Water Act prohibits unpermitted additions of pollutants to navigable waters from any point source. This prohibition is not limited to pollutants that flow directly from a point source to navigable waters. The word \"directly\" is nowhere in the text."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: -- what about the Fourth Circuit test? I take it you are advancing the Ninth Circuit fairly traceable test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Henkin",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HENKIN: Justice Ginsburg, in our view, our test is narrower. Direct hydrologic connection is the test that EPA and -- and -- and states had applied for three decades until EPA changed its position in April."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I'm not sure I really see much of a distinction between the direct hydrological connection or a hydrological connection and what you're --and what you're advocating."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Now traceability and causation don't quite seem to do it. So I wonder if you have any sort of fall-back position there that -- that would cure my worry without getting into the evasion problems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: -- could you say that as to a septic tank?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Henkin, you have been asked in various forms the question that was put in the reply brief on page 11, and it is: Would you require permits for a toilet, an identifiable point source, that originates wastewater and foreseeably sends it to the county's wells? So how do you answer that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I mean, do you think that that's really comparable, where you have a pipe that's over the river and the pollutant is coming out of the river and going through the air, that anybody's going to seriously argue that, well, because it went through the air, it wasn't covered?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But --but\nCongress knew about the ground -- groundwater\nissue and there were debates about this precise\ngroundwater issue, maybe not this precise, but\nthe groundwater issue, and there were proposals,\nas you're well aware, and some of the amicus\nbriefs go through this at great length, to put\nin regulation of groundwater, and Congress\nrejected those.\nSo how do we assess that in thinking\nabout this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Henkin",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HENKIN: -- they said we recognize\nthe essential link between ground and surface\nwaters and the artificial nature of any\ndistinction.\nIf Congress had wanted to say point\nsource discharge that reaches the navigable\nwaters through groundwater is exempt, because we\nwant to leave that completely to the states,\nthey would have said that in the language of the\nAct. They didn't."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Henkin",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HENKIN: Well, there are examples\nin the EPA official's brief in which delegated\nstates are regulating those sources of pollution\nby using the NPDES permit program."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: The preventive\nmeasures of this law were not followed and\nsomething failed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-260",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4fbfc238bdfc0be91d4d1b8d78365642789561ed34920cddaf1b2db835bdd319",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fbfc238bdfc-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you,\ncounsel. The case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 11:06 a.m., the case\nwas submitted.)"
    },
